 "summary": "Ledger POST in finalize() is not idempotent \u2014 only connect-phase retries are safe",
 "content": "Invoice finalization talks to the external ledger service and is the most sensitive call in src/billing/invoices.py. The ledger endpoint has no idempotency key, so sending the posting twice double-posts the invoice. Do not add general retries (read timeouts, resets after send, 5xx). The posting may already have landed. The only retries are on the _ledger session (urllib3 Retry with connect=3, everything else 0). Those cover failures to establish a connection, where the request was never sent. Caveat: finalize_once() only guards invoices that already have ledger_ref. ledger_ref is set only after a successful response, so it does NOT protect against a timed-out-but-posted attempt.",
 "invalidated_by": [
  "src/billing/invoices.py"
 ],
 "premise": "while the ledger API lacks an idempotency key"
}
